<title>FRANCE: Eiffage stock rises on Danish contract.</title>
<headline>Eiffage stock rises on Danish contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Eiffage extended the previous day's 7.3 percent rise on Wednesday on reports that it had obtained a Danish subway contract, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 15 francs at 381 francs at 1130 GMT.</p>
<p>French newspapers said a consortium to which it belongs had won a state contract for the construction of a subway next year in Copenhagen.</p>
<p>Traders said the share was also recovering from a sharp slide since May when it was trading above 700 francs.</p>
<p>Eiffage confirmed the contract but gave no financial details.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
